# Per-package USE for the live image (stage1 and stage2 share this confdir).
net-misc/networkmanager dhcpcd -dhclient
sys-kernel/linux-firmware initramfs
x11-base/xorg-server udev
dev-libs/libdbusmenu gtk3
sys-boot/grub mount
sys-apps/i2c-tools python
media-libs/libwebp -tiff
# RAM test boot entry. Catalyst copies /boot/memtest86plus/* (memtest64.bios and
# memtest.efi64) to the ISO root and the project's grub.cfg offers them.
sys-apps/memtest86+ boot bios64 uefi64
# Thin-provisioned LVM volumes are common on Fedora/RHEL and server installs; the
# repair tool cannot activate them without thin_check (thin-provisioning-tools).
# thin requires lvm (REQUIRED_USE), so both are named here.
sys-fs/lvm2 lvm thin
# mount must never depend on a library that is installed after it: with cryptsetup,
# util-linux links mount to libcryptsetup, which cannot be merged before lvm2, while every
# source build (lvm2 included) needs mount for Portage's namespace sandbox. Nothing on the
# live image uses mount's dm-verity support; the cryptsetup tool itself is unaffected.
sys-apps/util-linux -cryptsetup
# The live image keeps AIO cooler support in HWMonux (the ebuild leaves it off by default
# because liquidctl is ~amd64) and Secure Boot signing tools for the installer's checks.
app-misc/hwmonux liquidctl
# safe-graphics installs the kernel configuration fragment for the live kernel (see the stage2 spec).
app-admin/gentoo-live-installer secureboot safe-graphics
# The live desktop's look (wave 5): the Arc GTK and xfwm4 themes, without the GTK 2 theme (it would
# pull gtk-engines-murrine and gnome-themes-standard for programs the disc does not have).
x11-themes/arc-theme xfce -gtk2
# The AI rescue stick (wave 6): ttyd shares the rescue session to a phone over TLS, so it needs
# libwebsockets with libuv and OpenSSL support (the ttyd ebuild requires [libuv,ssl]).
net-libs/libwebsockets libuv ssl
